    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **264 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome`. (The stack trace glimpsed earlier was log output from `createUserNoRolesFails`, which deliberately exercises a failure path and still passes.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:74-75`), matching the pattern of the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome line on successful create** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:268`), right after the owner is persisted and its audit event is emitted, but before the `201 Created` response is returned:\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome: ownerId={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThis fires only on the successful-create path (all the earlier validation/limit branches return before it, and the idempotent-replay path returns `200 OK` earlier without re-enqueuing), and the emitted line contains both the owner id and the memberId \u2014 satisfying the acceptance test's `notify.anyContains(String.valueOf(id), memberId)` assertion.",
